On August 31, the opening day of the 6th World Nomad Games, free shuttle buses will transport spectators to Bishkek Arena from 2 p.m. to 4 p.m., the Bishkek City Hall reported.
The municipality said spectators will be able to reach the stadium by special transport from 21 locations across the capital. The last shuttle will depart at 4 p.m., so city authorities recommend arriving at the nearest departure point in advance.
Shuttle buses will be available to spectators with tickets to the official opening ceremony of the 6th World Nomad Games or invitations to the event.
Departure points:
- Intersection of Ibraimov and Frunze streets;
- Intersection of Zhibek Zholu Avenue and Kuliev Street, former Western bus station;
- 32 Barpy Alykulov Street, Kirkomstroy;
- 3/7 A. Tokombaev Street, Asanbai microdistrict;
- Ak-Kula bus station, Kozhomkul village, 13B/1 Frunze Street;
- 4 Auezov Street, Alamedin-1 microdistrict;
- Terminal stop in Tunguch microdistrict, 64/1;
- 10A/1 Aul Street, Kozhzavod;
- 263/2 Zhibek Zholu Avenue, former Eastern bus station;
- Intersection of Isa Akhunbaev and Dostoevsky streets, Kok-Zhar residential area;
- 98/1 Altymyshev Street;
- 1/6 Ala-Archa Street, Baytik village, Globus;
- 1/A Erkindik Boulevard, railway station;
- 287 Imanaly Aidarbekov Street;
- 275/6 Maldybayev Street, Youth Quarter;
- 52 Shabdan Baatyr Street, Depot-2;
- 239 Moskovskaya Street, terminal stop of electric bus No. 4, Depot-1;
- 209 Deng Xiaoping Avenue;
- Timur Frunze Street, Institute of Agriculture;
- 115 Ala-Too Street, Ala-Too residential area;
- 16 Tynaliev Street.
After the ceremony, spectators will be able to return on the same shuttle buses.
The 6th World Nomad Games will be held in Kyrgyzstan from August 31 to September 6, 2026. The opening ceremony will take place in Bishkek on August 31, while the main competitions will be held in Issyk-Kul region.
